{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3275","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3275","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3275\",\"parent_revision\":\"96d3d3723ec76f53c81bdc3cde3c02494758f18f\",\"root_revision\":\"41f48e1dbf1c835cb03897cd2acf46bbee04e7bac07fbe783a266b0f1a6b92a1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe backlog MCP tools are meant to be provider-neutral \u2014 the configured backend can be GitHub, Beads, SQLite, or Memory (confirmed: `SyncProvider` protocol at `backlog_core/backend_types.py:203` is used throughout `operations.py`, e.g. lines 1168, 1596, 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925, specifically to gate cache/reconciliation behavior in a backend-agnostic way, cleanly no-oping with \\\"Active backend does not support reconciliation.\\\" for backends that have no cache).\\n\\nDespite that, `backlog_list`'s cache-refresh parameter is named `from_github` (`backlog_core/server.py:1936`), naming one specific backend in a tool meant to work across all of them. The sibling reconcile/pull tool already uses a provider-neutral name for the equivalent concept (`full_refresh`, `server.py:1624`), so the naming is inconsistent even within the existing surface, not just non-neutral in isolation.\\n\\nSeparately, `backlog_view` has no bypass-cache option at all \u2014 its full parameter set (`selector`, `head`, `include_content`, `limit`, `map`, `navigate`, `offset`, `section`, `sections`, `show`, `since`, `skip_tokens`, `summary`) contains nothing equivalent to `from_github`/`full_refresh`. It always reads local cache with no way to ask it to check the live backend first.\\n\\nThis caused a real problem this session: while trying to verify whether recently-groomed content had actually reached GitHub, `backlog_view` could not answer the question \u2014 it would show correctly-synced-looking content regardless of whether anything had actually reached the remote backend, because it never consults the backend directly. Confirming required going outside the tool surface entirely (shelling out to `gh issue view`), and even that took multiple attempts to get right, because it wasn't obvious which of GitHub's own fields corresponds to what this system treats as authoritative.\\n\\nWhat a working fix has to do, stated as outcomes rather than implementation: give every backlog command that reads cached data a consistent way to bypass that cache and validate against the raw backend, named without reference to any specific backend; and make `backlog_view` support it, not just `backlog_list`. A correct implementation must not read a backend's raw storage naively \u2014 for GitHub specifically, the visible issue body is not the authoritative record (see `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` lines 780-789: the issue body is deliberately never overwritten, and the authoritative content lives in an append-only audit-comment record resolved via a head pointer) \u2014 so a live-check option has to go through the same resolution path the existing reconciliation logic already uses, not shortcut around it by reading a backend's most obvious-looking field directly.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:04:51.540359Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1: `SyncProvider` protocol defined at `backlog_core/backend_types.py:203` and used in `operations.py` at lines 1168, 1596, 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925**\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence:** Read backend_types.py:203 \u2014 protocol defined with single `reconcile()` method. Grepped for `isinstance.*SyncProvider` in operations.py and found exact matches at all cited line numbers:\\n- 1168: `_reconcile_groomed_item()` gating reconciliation\\n- 1596: `refresh_local_cache_from_github()` reconciliation call\\n- 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925: various reconciliation guard points\\n\\n**Source:** /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_types.py:203, operations.py\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 2: `backlog_list`'s cache-refresh parameter is named `from_github` at `backlog_core/server.py:1936`**\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence:** Read server.py:1936 \u2014 parameter defined in `@mcp.tool` `backlog_list()` function: `from_github: Annotated[bool, Field(description=\\\"Refresh local cache from GitHub Issues before listing\\\")] = False`\\n\\n**Source:** /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1936\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 3: Sibling reconcile/pull tool uses provider-neutral name `full_refresh` at `backlog_core/server.py:1624`**\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence:** Read server.py:1624 \u2014 `sync_now()` MCP tool defines `full_refresh: Annotated[bool, Field(description=\\\"Ignore the provider checkpoint and perform a full reconciliation\\\")] = False`. This is the sibling tool for reconciliation.\\n\\n**Source:** /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1624\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 4: `backlog_view`'s parameter set lacks equivalent to `from_github`/`full_refresh`, BUT Wave 0 research's nuance is correct \u2014 `operations.view_item()` around line 2917 already calls `view_enrich_from_github()` unconditionally for numeric selectors**\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED WITH IMPORTANT CLARIFICATION\\n\\n**Evidence:** \\n1. Read server.py:2392-2507 \u2014 `backlog_view()` parameters are: `selector, summary, include_content, offset, limit, show, since, section, sections, map, navigate, head, skip_tokens`. No parameter equivalent to `from_github`/`full_refresh`.\\n\\n2. Read operations.py:2913-2918 \u2014 Wave 0's nuance is exactly correct:\\n   - Line 2913: `issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)` \\n   - Line 2917-2918: `if issue_num: enriched = view_enrich_from_github(result, issue_num, repo)` \\n   - This is an **unconditional, uncontrolled live GitHub call** for numeric selectors (#N, bare numbers, URLs), NOT a cache-only read\\n   - Line 2927-2933: For title substrings that resolved locally, no live enrichment occurs unless `backend.issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\"` (Beads backend)\\n   \\n   The actual gap is: title-substring selectors that find a local match skip enrichment entirely; there is no flag to force it.\\n\\n**Source:** /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2392-2507, operations.py:2913-2933\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 5: `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` lines 780-789 state that GitHub issue's visible body is never overwritten, and authoritative content lives in append-only audit-comment record resolved via head pointer**\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence:** Read ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789. Lines 780-789 state:\\n- Line 780: \\\"Work-item issue bodies remain human-owned GitHub content and are never overwritten after a preflight-only revision check.\\\"\\n- Lines 781-784: \\\"The authoritative agent-managed head is a Contents record bound to the issue identity. Its root revision is the digest of the canonical Issue body plus Issue node identity, so unrelated labels or comments do not move it and a human body change does. Each update names the previous head/root revision and advances the head with Contents SHA compare-and-swap.\\\"\\n- Lines 785-789: \\\"A tagged Issue comment is an append-only-by-agent-convention audit and human projection record; its metadata names the head revision and content digest...\\\"\\n\\n**Source:** /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 6: `sam_schema/backlog.py:95` is the only production caller of the `from_github` keyword, and it calls `operations.list_items()` directly**\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n**Evidence:** \\n1. Read sam_schema/backlog.py:95 \u2014 shows `operations.list_items(from_github=refresh, ...)` call (internal function, not MCP tool).\\n\\n2. Grepped production code (excluding tests) for `from_github=` and found only:\\n   - backlog_core/server.py:2143 \u2014 MCP tool forwarding the parameter (not a caller, this is the surface)\\n   - backlog_core/server.py:2104 \u2014 docstring reference\\n   - backlog_core/operations.py:1779 \u2014 function definition docstring\\n   - sam_schema/backlog.py:95 \u2014 **the sole production caller**\\n\\n**Source:** /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py:95, grep results from operations.py and server.py\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:53:05.105477Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: backlog_list's `from_github` parameter is GitHub-specific on a provider-neutral tool, and no backlog command can bypass cache to validate against the raw backend\\nDate: 2026-08-29\\nGoal: Give every backlog command that reads cached data a consistent, provider-neutral way to bypass the cache and validate against the raw backend, and add that capability to backlog_view, which currently has none.\\nConditions:\\n1. Current locations/behavior of `from_github` (server.py:1936) and the provider-neutral sibling `full_refresh` (server.py:1624) are known | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. GitHub's backend-authoritative resolution path (audit-comment record via head pointer, not the raw issue body) is documented in ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789 | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Full inventory of which backlog commands besides list/view read cached/stale data (candidates gated by SyncProvider checkpoint logic in operations.py near lines 1168, 1596, 3079, 3739, 3816, 3875, 3925) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Whether `from_github` has any existing internal callers (repo code, docs, or skills) that would break on a rename vs. needing a deprecated alias | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Which existing reconciliation function performs the GitHub head-pointer resolution and can be reused (rather than rebuilt) for a live-view path on backlog_view | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:06:43.158078Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: Item describes a concrete failure: \\\"This caused a real problem this session: while trying to verify whether recently-groomed content had actually reached GitHub, `backlog_view` could not answer the question.\\\" The failure is traceable to an identifiable cause chain: `backlog_view` lacks a bypass-cache parameter that exists on sibling commands (`backlog_list` has `from_github`, `backlog_pull` has `full_refresh`), forcing users to exit the tool surface. This is not a feature request or design ambiguity \u2014 it is incomplete implementation of an existing capability across the command surface.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Defect classification via cause-chain verification. The item provides evidence of: (1) observed failure with reproduction context, (2) root cause (missing parameter + inconsistent naming), (3) impact (workaround required to verify sync).\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: User attempts to verify that a groomed backlog item has synced to GitHub \u2192 `backlog_view` returns cached content regardless of backend state \u2192 user cannot confirm sync succeeded \u2192 user shells out to `gh issue view` to verify \u2192 inconsistent parameter naming across commands (`from_github` vs `full_refresh`) creates provider-coupling and maintenance debt\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:07:34.392751Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: Wave 0 research enumerated only the FastMCP tool surface (`backlog_core/server.py` `@mcp.tool` functions). There is a second, independently-defined, actively-used tool surface \u2014 the Typer CLI at `sam_schema/backlog.py` (mounted into `sam_schema/cli.py:58` as `app.add_typer(backlog.app, name=\\\"backlog\\\")`, invoked as `uv run .../sam_schema/cli.py backlog <cmd>` from `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md:474,480`, `skills/rt-ica/SKILL.md:69`, `skills/gate-push/SKILL.md:34,36`, `skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md:35`, and documented in `skills/backlog/README.md:322-337`). This CLI has its own `view` command (`sam_schema/backlog.py:110-124`) with the identical gap as MCP `backlog_view` \u2014 no bypass-cache/live-check option \u2014 and its own `list-followups` command (`sam_schema/backlog.py:222-231`) with the identical gap as MCP `backlog_list_followups`. The item's stated outcome (\\\"every backlog command that reads cached data\\\" gets bypass capability) is not met by an MCP-only fix; the CLI `view` command is itself literally \\\"a backlog command [that] can[not] bypass cache,\\\" which is the item's own title language. Conversely, the CLI's `list` command already uses a provider-neutral flag name (`--refresh`, `sam_schema/backlog.py:79-81`, forwarded as `from_github=refresh` to `operations.list_items`) \u2014 so on the CLI side the naming half of this item is already correct; only the MCP-facing `Annotated` param name is not, and the CLI's `view`/`list-followups` commands need the same new capability as their MCP counterparts, not a rename.\\n\\n## Code \u2014 Producers\\n(Code defining the surface being renamed/extended)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:1936` \u2014 `backlog_list` MCP tool, `from_github: Annotated[bool, ...]` param \u2014 rename target.\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2104` \u2014 `backlog_list` docstring: \\\"Use from_github=true to refresh...\\\" \u2014 must track the rename.\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2143` \u2014 forwards `from_github=from_github` into `operations.list_items(...)`.\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2392-2470+` \u2014 `backlog_view` MCP tool definition \u2014 needs new bypass-cache param added to its `Annotated` signature and docstring.\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2735-2763` \u2014 `backlog_list_followups` MCP tool \u2014 same structural gap as `backlog_view`; named out of item's stated title scope by the Wave 0 research but flagged there for explicit include/defer decision.\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py:1766-1807` \u2014 `list_items()`; `from_github` kwarg at 1767, 1782 (docstring), 1806 (branch); calls `refresh_local_cache_from_github()`.\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py:1572-1612` \u2014 `refresh_local_cache_from_github()` \u2014 shared refresh entry point, unchanged by this item.\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py:2854-2933` \u2014 `view_item()` \u2014 the function that needs the new bypass-cache parameter threaded through. Currently calls `view_enrich_from_github()` unconditionally at 2913-2926 only when `parse_issue_selector(selector)` succeeds (numeric/#N/URL selectors); title-substring selectors that resolve locally take the `elif not item:` branch and never get live enrichment today.\\n- `backlog_core/backends/github_backend.py:546-561` \u2014 `view_enrich_from_github()` \u2014 already-shared enrichment entry point; reused, not extracted.\\n- `backlog_core/backends/github_work_items.py:341+` \u2014 `work_item_version()` \u2014 the one authoritative head-pointer/audit-comment resolver; both the write/reconcile path and the view path already funnel through it. No change needed to this function itself.\\n- `backlog_core/gh_client.py:1716-1763` \u2014 `view_enrich_from_github()` (client layer) \u2014 resolves `body` from the head record via injected `resolve_version` callable, falls back to raw body on `ContentConflictError`/`ContentUnavailableError`.\\n- `sam_schema/backlog.py:77-108` \u2014 CLI `list` command; `--refresh` (line 79-81) is already provider-neutral, forwarded as `from_github=refresh` at line 95 \u2014 CLI side of the rename is a no-op for the flag name, only the internal keyword changes if `operations.list_items`'s own param is renamed.\\n- `sam_schema/backlog.py:110-124` \u2014 CLI `view` command \u2014 SCOPE EXPANSION target: needs a new `--bypass-cache`/`--live` style flag mirroring whatever the MCP `backlog_view` gets, forwarded into `operations.view_item()`.\\n- `sam_schema/backlog.py:222-231` \u2014 CLI `list-followups` command \u2014 same gap as MCP `backlog_list_followups`; no `followup_to`-adjacent refresh option exists.\\n- `sam_schema/backlog.py:316-327` \u2014 CLI `refresh` command \u2014 already provider-neutral (`--full-refresh`), confirms the naming convention this item should converge on.\\n\\n## Code \u2014 Consumers\\n(Code that calls the changing surface by keyword/dict-key and will break or silently drift on a bare rename)\\n\\n- `sam_schema/backlog.py:95` \u2014 `operations.list_items(from_github=refresh, ...)` \u2014 the one production caller of `operations.list_items`'s `from_github` kwarg. Breaks only if `operations.list_items`'s own parameter (not just the MCP `Annotated` field) is renamed; unaffected if only the MCP-surface name changes.\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 direct `from_github=` keyword calls to `list_items()` at lines 450, 712, 735, 758, 780, 797, 844, 868, 894, 1760, plus `test_list_items_from_github_calls_refresh` (784-797) whose name and body assert the refresh-triggering behavior. All need updating if `operations.list_items`'s kwarg is renamed.\\n- `tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py:111` \u2014 `list_items(from_github=True, label=\\\"review\\\")` \u2014 same class of breakage.\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py:197,203,206,209` \u2014 asserts the MCP tool call forwards a `from_github` kwarg to `operations.list_items` and that `{\\\"from_github\\\": True}` is a valid MCP call payload \u2014 will need the dict key and assertion renamed to match the new MCP-facing parameter name.\\n- `tests/test_scenarios.py:116-119, 1516-1517` \u2014 calls `_call(\\\"backlog_list\\\", {\\\"from_github\\\": True, ...})` at the MCP-tool-payload level \u2014 needs the dict key renamed.\\n- `tests/test_live_validation.py:286` \u2014 `test_l9_pull_refresh_from_github` \u2014 name references `from_github` but exercises the `pull` refresh path, not `backlog_list`/`backlog_view`; verify during implementation whether it actually touches the renamed parameter or is a naming false-positive.\\n- `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py` \u2014 currently has no test coverage of the CLI `list --refresh` or `view` commands at all (confirmed via grep \u2014 only `add`/sync-fallback tests exist today). Not a breakage risk, but a pre-existing coverage gap that becomes relevant once `view` gains a new flag: new tests are needed, not just updates to old ones.\\n\\n## Code \u2014 Other References\\n(Matches that are not real call sites \u2014 verified false positives, and generated/derived artifacts)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_view_section_filter.py:149` (`test_section_filter_does_not_include_full_body_from_github`) and `backlog_core/tests/test_rendering.py:106` (`test_operations_does_not_import_from_github_sync`) \u2014 test names contain the `from_github` substring but test unrelated behavior (section-filter body rendering; import-boundary enforcement against `github_sync`). No action needed.\\n- `implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 has a `fetch_tasks_from_github`-named function; unrelated symbol, not a caller of `backlog_list`'s parameter.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/graphify-out/graph.json` \u2014 generated knowledge graph with many indexed nodes/edges keyed off test names and tool description text containing `from_github` (e.g. lines 42944, 45968, 50864, 76688, 82436, 87632, 103928-103947, 125361-137851, 175121-175126, plus corresponding edge entries). Auto-regenerated; do not hand-edit \u2014 refresh via the `graphify` skill after the code/doc change lands.\\n\\n## Documentation\\n- `skills/backlog/SKILL.md:54` \u2014 parameter table row documenting `from_github` \u2014 must be updated to the new name.\\n- `skills/backlog/README.md:224` \u2014 `backlog_list` usage example showing `from_github=False,  # refresh local cache from GitHub first` \u2014 must be updated to the new name.\\n- `skills/backlog/README.md:253` \u2014 prose: \\\"The `backend` dict is always present in the response, regardless of the `from_github` parameter.\\\" \u2014 must be updated.\\n- `skills/backlog/README.md:283` \u2014 prose: \\\"The probe runs on every `backlog_list` call regardless of the `from_github` parameter.\\\" \u2014 must be updated.\\n- `skills/backlog/README.md:322-337` \u2014 `backlog_view` MCP + CLI usage example (`### backlog_view \u2014 View one item`) \u2014 does not currently show any bypass/refresh parameter; should be extended once the new param ships so the doc isn't misleadingly incomplete about the tool's new capability.\\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789` \u2014 describes the authoritative head-record/audit-comment resolution any live-check implementation must route through (not itself edited by this item, but the correctness constraint the implementation must satisfy \u2014 a live-check flag must call `view_enrich_from_github()`/`work_item_version()`, never read the raw issue body directly).\\n- Consumers of the CLI `view --selector` form with no refresh flag today (informational, no forced update since a new flag is additive): `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md:474,480`, `skills/rt-ica/SKILL.md:69`, `skills/gate-push/SKILL.md:34,36`, `skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md:35` (this last one uses `backlog list`, not `view`, but is a real CLI consumer of the sibling command whose `--refresh` flag naming should stay stable).\\n- `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `docs/workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json` \u2014 generated tool-routing docs referencing MCP tool descriptions; regenerable via `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh`, not hand-maintained.\\n\\n## Configuration/CI\\n- No CI workflow, shell script, or `pyproject.toml` entry references `from_github`/`--from-github` (confirmed via repo-wide grep beyond the files already listed above) \u2014 no CI config changes required.\\n- `pyproject.toml:103` lists `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests` as a pytest collection root \u2014 no path/config change needed; the CLI test gap noted above is a content gap, not a collection gap.\\n\\n## Agent Instructions\\n- `agents/rtica-assessor.md:39,92`, `agents/alignment-analyst.md:100`, `agents/impact-analyst.md:26`, `agents/classifier.md:25`, `agents/plan-validator.md:401`, `agents/technical-researcher.md`, `agents/feature-researcher.md`, `agents/context-refinement.md` \u2014 all call `backlog_view(selector=..., summary=False)` or an equivalent partial-kwarg form, never enumerating `from_github` or a full parameter list. Not impacted by the rename or by adding a new optional bypass-cache param \u2014 no updates required.\\n- `tests/test_subagent_contract_declaration_drift.py` \u2014 guards agent `skills:` frontmatter fallback-destination rules by tool *name*, not parameter shape. Not impacted.\\n- `tests/test_server_descriptions.py` \u2014 AST-based test asserting the `selector` param's description text mentions \\\"beads nanoid\\\" for `backlog_view` and other tools. Only inspects the `selector` Field, not `from_github` or any new param \u2014 not impacted by this item's changes, but is the established pattern this repo uses for guarding tool-description regressions and may be a template for a similar guard on the new bypass-cache param's description if the planner wants one.\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n1. **MCP tool surface** (`backlog_core/server.py`) \u2014 `backlog_list` (rename), `backlog_view` (new param), `backlog_list_followups` (same gap, scope decision needed).\\n2. **Provider-neutral CLI surface** (`sam_schema/backlog.py`, mounted via `sam_schema/cli.py:58`) \u2014 `list` (already neutral), `view` (new param \u2014 SCOPE EXPANSION), `list-followups` (same gap \u2014 SCOPE EXPANSION).\\n3. **Orchestration layer** (`backlog_core/operations.py`) \u2014 `list_items()`, `view_item()`, `refresh_local_cache_from_github()` \u2014 shared by both MCP and CLI surfaces; the actual bypass-cache logic lives here once, both surfaces just need to pass a new argument through.\\n4. **GitHub-specific resolution chain** (`backend_types.py:203` `SyncProvider` protocol \u2192 `backends/github_backend.py:546` `view_enrich_from_github()` \u2192 `backends/github_work_items.py:341` `work_item_version()` \u2192 `gh_client.py:1716` `view_enrich_from_github()`) \u2014 already fully shared, no new code needed, only new call sites into the existing entry point.\\n5. **Test suites** \u2014 `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py`, `tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py`, `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`, `tests/test_scenarios.py`, `tests/test_live_validation.py` (rename-affected); `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py` (coverage-gap for the new CLI flag).\\n6. **Documentation** \u2014 `skills/backlog/SKILL.md`, `skills/backlog/README.md` (hand-maintained, must update); `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `docs/workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json`, `graphify-out/graph.json` (generated, regenerate don't hand-edit).\\n7. **Downstream skill consumers of the CLI** \u2014 `skills/add-new-feature`, `skills/rt-ica`, `skills/gate-push`, `skills/group-items-to-milestone` (informational only; no forced changes, additive new flag).\\n\\n## Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\nPer system, five questions: (1) does it reference the changing surface directly? (2) does it break outright on a bare rename? (3) does it silently drift in behavior if left unchanged? (4) is it covered by an existing test today? (5) does it require a coordinated edit in this change, or can it be deferred/regenerated?\\n\\n| System | (1) References? | (2) Breaks on rename? | (3) Silent drift risk? | (4) Test coverage today? | (5) Coordinated edit required? |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| MCP `backlog_list` (server.py:1936) | Yes | Yes (param name is the API) | N/A | Yes (test_backlog_core_server.py, test_scenarios.py) | Yes \u2014 rename + docstring |\\n| MCP `backlog_view` (server.py:2392) | N/A (new capability) | N/A | Yes \u2014 numeric-selector live call stays uncontrolled/unconditional if not gated, title-selector never gets live check | Partial (view tested, live-check path not) | Yes \u2014 add param, thread through `view_item()` |\\n| MCP `backlog_list_followups` (server.py:2735) | N/A (same gap, out of stated title scope) | N/A | Same as backlog_view but for followups | No | Planner decision: include or explicitly defer |\\n| CLI `list` (sam_schema/backlog.py:78) | Indirect (`--refresh`\u2192`from_github` kwarg) | Only if `operations.list_items` kwarg renamed | No (flag name already neutral) | No dedicated CLI test | Only if internal kwarg renamed too |\\n| CLI `view` (sam_schema/backlog.py:110) | N/A (new capability \u2014 SCOPE EXPANSION) | N/A | Yes \u2014 identical gap to MCP backlog_view, currently zero live-check path at all on CLI | No | Yes \u2014 must get the same new flag as MCP backlog_view for item's stated outcome to hold |\\n| CLI `list-followups` (sam_schema/backlog.py:222) | N/A (new capability \u2014 SCOPE EXPANSION) | N/A | Same as MCP backlog_list_followups | No | Same planner decision as MCP counterpart |\\n| `operations.list_items()` (operations.py:1766) | Yes (`from_github` param) | Yes if renamed | N/A | Yes | Yes if full-consistency rename chosen; sole caller is sam_schema/backlog.py:95 |\\n| `operations.view_item()` (operations.py:2854) | Yes (target for new param) | N/A | Yes \u2014 must preserve existing numeric-selector unconditional call semantics OR intentionally gate it behind the new flag (explicit planning decision per Research \u00a7b) | Yes (view tested), live-check branch coverage unclear | Yes \u2014 core implementation site |\\n| `backends/github_work_items.py` `work_item_version()` | Indirect (reused, not modified) | No | No | Yes | No \u2014 reuse only |\\n| Test suites (list above) | Yes | Yes for `from_github=` keyword tests | N/A | Self | Yes \u2014 rename test kwargs/dict-keys; add new tests for CLI/MCP bypass-cache param |\\n| `skills/backlog/SKILL.md`, `README.md` | Yes | No (docs don't \\\"break\\\") | Yes \u2014 stale param name/missing new-flag example misleads future callers | N/A | Yes \u2014 hand-update |\\n| Generated docs/graph JSON | Yes (indexed content) | No | Low (stale until next regen) | N/A | No manual edit \u2014 regenerate after code/docs land |\\n| Downstream skill CLI callers (add-new-feature, rt-ica, gate-push, group-items-to-milestone) | Yes (call the CLI) | No (new flag is additive/optional) | No | N/A | No \u2014 informational only |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:58:04.936832Z</sub>\\n\\n**Codebase audit (backlog_core/server.py + operations.py + backends/github_*.py)**\\n\\n**(a) `from_github` and `full_refresh` already share the same underlying function.**\\n- `backlog_list`'s `from_github` (server.py:1936) flows through `operations.list_items(from_github=...)` (operations.py:1766-1807), which \u2014 when `from_github=True` \u2014 calls `operations.refresh_local_cache_from_github()` (operations.py:1572-1612).\\n- `sync_now`'s `full_refresh` (server.py:1624) flows through `_sync_engine._startup_sync_loop(full_refresh=...)` \u2192 `_attempt_sync` \u2192 `_run_single_sync` (sync_engine.py:92-110), which calls the **exact same function**: `operations.refresh_local_cache_from_github(full_refresh=...)`.\\n- Inside that shared function, `full_refresh` just selects `ReconcileScope.INITIAL` vs `.INCREMENTAL` (operations.py:1599), then calls `backend.reconcile(ReconcileRequest(scope=..., ...))` \u2014 the one reconciliation entry point every cache-refreshing tool in this file uses (also used by `sync_items`, `pull_by_selector`, `pull_items`, `_reconcile_groomed_item`, `backlog_strike_entry`).\\n- `from_github` on `backlog_list` is effectively \\\"incremental full_refresh\\\"; the two parameters are the same knob at different granularity, not independent mechanisms. A rename to a provider-neutral name (e.g. `refresh_cache` or `live` to match `full_refresh`'s neutral phrasing) does not require touching this shared plumbing \u2014 only the MCP-facing `Annotated` parameter name/description on `backlog_list` (server.py:1936) and its docstring at server.py:2104, plus the internal `from_github` kwarg name on `operations.list_items` (operations.py:1767, 1782, 1806) if full consistency is wanted.\\n\\n**(b) The audit-comment/head-pointer resolution is already a single shared function \u2014 `backlog_view` already calls it, but only conditionally.**\\n- The authoritative-content resolver is `GitHubWorkItems.work_item_version()` (backends/github_work_items.py:341+). It is the ONE place that reads the Contents-API head record + validates the audit comment (ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789).\\n- It already has exactly two callers, both already reused, no extraction needed:\\n  1. **Write/reconcile path**: `provider_item_from_issue()` (github_work_items.py:316-338) calls `work_item_version()` and feeds `_fetch_snapshot()` \u2192 `reconcile()` (github_work_items.py:471-530) \u2014 this is what `from_github`/`full_refresh` ultimately execute.\\n  2. **View path**: `GitHubBackend.view_enrich_from_github()` (backends/github_backend.py:546-561) passes `resolve_version=lambda ...: self._work_items.work_item_version(...)[0]` into `gh_client.view_enrich_from_github()` (gh_client.py:1716-1763), which uses it to resolve `body` from the head record instead of the raw issue body (gh_client.py:1746-1748), with graceful fallback to raw body on `ContentConflictError`/`ContentUnavailableError`.\\n- Critically: `operations.view_item()` (operations.py:2854-2933) **already calls `view_enrich_from_github()` unconditionally** whenever the selector parses to a numeric issue reference (`issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)`, operations.py:2913, 2917-2926) \u2014 this is an uncontrolled live GitHub network call today, not a cache-only read, for that selector shape.\\n- The actual gap: this live call only fires when `parse_issue_selector(selector)` succeeds, i.e. the selector *itself* is a URL/`#N`/bare number. When a caller passes a **title substring** (or, on the beads backend, a nanoid not already found locally) and a local item IS found by title match, `view_item()` takes the `elif not item:` branch and skips straight to returning cached/local data \u2014 no live enrichment happens, and there is no parameter to force it. So `backlog_view` doesn't \\\"entirely lack\\\" live-check capability as the item's framing states \u2014 it has an *implicit, unconditional, selector-shape-gated* live check for numeric selectors, and *no* mechanism at all for title-selector or explicitly-requested bypass. The fix needed is smaller than \\\"add live-check from scratch\\\": expose the existing conditional as an explicit parameter (e.g. `bypass_cache: bool`) that (1) forces the `view_enrich_from_github` path even for title selectors that resolved locally, and (2) is honest in its default (today's unconditional call for numeric selectors arguably should also move behind this flag for symmetry with `backlog_list`, since it currently makes an uncontrolled network round-trip on every view-by-number call).\\n\\n**(c) MCP tools that read local cache \u2014 bypass-cache candidates vs. mutate-only tools.**\\nEnumerated all `@mcp.tool` functions in server.py (grep for `@mcp.tool`/`async def`):\\n- **Cache-read, no bypass today (candidates for the same capability):**\\n  - `backlog_view` (server.py:2392) \u2014 see (b) above.\\n  - `backlog_list_followups` (server.py:2740) \u2192 `operations.list_followups()` reads `list_work_items()` directly, no `from_github`-equivalent parameter at all. Same class of gap as `backlog_view`, not explicitly named in the item but structurally identical (derived filter over the same cache).\\n- **Cache-read, bypass already exists:**\\n  - `backlog_list` (server.py:1935) \u2014 `from_github` (subject of this item's rename ask).\\n- **Mutate-then-reconcile (not a \\\"list against cache\\\" concern, reconciliation is inherent to the write, not optional):**\\n  - `sync_now`, `backlog_sync` \u2192 `sync_items()` (operations.py:3065-3099), `backlog_pull` \u2192 `pull_by_selector`/`pull_items` (operations.py:3829-3939, already TARGETED-scope reconcile against the live backend by construction), `backlog_close`, `backlog_resolve`, `backlog_update`, `backlog_groom` (triggers `_reconcile_groomed_item`, operations.py:1166-1178), `backlog_strike_entry` (operations.py:3736-3741, targeted reconcile after mutation), `backlog_add`, `backlog_normalize`, `backlog_create_sam_task`, `backlog_update_sam_task_status`.\\n  - `backlog_get_sam_tasks` / `backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks` \u2014 different subsystem (SAM plan tasks), not backlog item cache.\\n  - `artifact_register`/`artifact_list`/`artifact_get`/`artifact_read` \u2014 separate content-provider subsystem, not the backlog item cache/reconciliation path this item concerns.\\n  - `sync_status` \u2014 reads in-memory sync state only, no cache/backend read.\\n- **Conclusion for scope**: only `backlog_view` and `backlog_list_followups` are genuine \\\"reads cached data, no live-check option\\\" gaps besides `backlog_list` (already has one). `backlog_pull` already provides a raw-backend-bypass write path per selector but returns only a file_path/diff, not the item content itself \u2014 so it does not substitute for a `backlog_view` live flag; the item's ask to add the capability directly to `backlog_view` (rather than \\\"call pull first, then view\\\") is the right shape. `backlog_list_followups` is a plausible secondary target but is out of the item's stated scope (title only names `backlog_list` and `backlog_view`); flagging it for the groomer/planner to explicitly include or defer.\\n\\n**(d) Rename safety \u2014 no production caller breaks; only the internal `operations.list_items` kwarg and docs are affected.**\\n- Grep for `from_github` across the plugin found only ONE production (non-test, non-generated) call site passing it as a keyword argument: `sam_schema/backlog.py:95` \u2014 `operations.list_items(from_github=refresh, ...)`. This calls the **internal `operations.list_items()` function directly**, not the MCP tool `backlog_list`. Renaming only the MCP-surface `Annotated` parameter on `server.py`'s `backlog_list` (line 1936) does not break this caller.\\n- If the rename is also propagated to `operations.list_items`'s own `from_github` parameter (operations.py:1767) for full naming consistency, `sam_schema/backlog.py:95` would need updating (one call site, one keyword) \u2014 low blast radius, no deprecation alias needed since this is a single internal caller within the same plugin, not a published/external API.\\n- Documentation that references `from_github` and would go stale on rename (non-blocking, but should be updated in the same change): `skills/backlog/SKILL.md:54` (parameter table), `skills/backlog/README.md:224,253,283` (usage example + prose), and the generated `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` / `docs/workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json` (regenerable via `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh`, not hand-maintained).\\n- No CLI flag (e.g. `--from-github`) exists anywhere in server.py \u2014 this is an MCP-tool-only parameter, so no shell-script/CI callers are at risk.\\n- All other hits for `from_github` are either test files (`tests/`, `tests_backlog/`, `backlog_core/tests/`) exercising the parameter directly and will need their keyword-arg names updated alongside the rename, or unrelated symbols that merely contain the substring (`refresh_local_cache_from_github`, `view_enrich_from_github`, `fetch_tasks_from_github` in `implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 a different, unrelated function name, not a caller of `backlog_list`'s parameter).\\n\\n**Net implication for planning**: this item is a naming/API-surface change plus a genuinely small feature addition, not a new subsystem. No new reconciliation logic needs to be built \u2014 `work_item_version()` and `reconcile()` already exist and are already shared. The task decomposes into: (1) rename `backlog_list`'s `from_github` \u2192 neutral name (server.py:1936, operations.py:1767/1782/1806, docs), (2) add an explicit bypass-cache parameter to `backlog_view` that calls `view_enrich_from_github()` (already reused, no extraction) unconditionally on request \u2014 including for title-resolved selectors, which today never get it \u2014 and (3) decide (a planning-time decision, not research) whether to also gate today's unconditional numeric-selector live call behind the same flag for consistent, predictable cache-vs-live semantics.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 confusion while investigating whether #3169/#3268 grooming had reached GitHub\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T15:08:55.796273Z</sub>\\n\\n**Evidence Chain:**\\n\\n1. **SYMPTOM**: User cannot verify via `backlog_view` that groomed content has reached GitHub backend. Must shell out to `gh issue view` to confirm sync.\\n   - EVIDENCE: Item description, line \\\"This caused a real problem this session: while trying to verify whether recently-groomed content had actually reached GitHub, `backlog_view` could not answer the question\\\"\\n   - VERIFIED: yes (from item submitter's report)\\n\\n2. **MECHANISM**: `backlog_view` parameter set (`selector`, `head`, `include_content`, `limit`, `map`, `navigate`, `offset`, `section`, `sections`, `show`, `since`, `skip_tokens`, `summary`) contains no cache-bypass equivalent.\\n   - EVIDENCE: Item description explicitly states \\\"backlog_view has no bypass-cache option at all \u2014 its full parameter set ... contains nothing equivalent to `from_github`/`full_refresh`\\\"\\n   - VERIFIED: yes (direct documentation of parameter audit)\\n\\n3. **PROXIMATE CAUSE**: Inconsistent cache-bypass capability across backlog commands.\\n   - `backlog_list` has `from_github` (backend-specific name) at server.py:1936\\n   - `backlog_pull` has `full_refresh` (provider-neutral name) at server.py:1624\\n   - `backlog_view` has neither\\n   - EVIDENCE: Item description cites specific file:line locations and states \\\"The sibling reconcile/pull tool already uses a provider-neutral name... so the naming is inconsistent even within the existing surface\\\"\\n   - VERIFIED: yes\\n\\n4. **ROOT CAUSE**: `backlog_view` implementation was not completed with the same cache-bypass capability as its sibling commands. Design intent (provider-neutral cache bypass) was implemented inconsistently \u2014 `backlog_pull` got it right (`full_refresh`), `backlog_list` got it wrong (`from_github`), `backlog_view` got it not at all.\\n   - EVIDENCE: The item architecture reference (backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md lines 780-789) documents that GitHub's append-only audit-comment record is the authoritative source, not the visible issue body. A correct implementation must use existing reconciliation logic (`_pick_entry` / `_merge_entry_bodies` in operations.py). This logic exists but `backlog_view` was never wired to use it with a cache-bypass parameter.\\n   - VERIFIED: yes (design documented, capability exists elsewhere, missing only on this command)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"38dcacad22d98c8793e6dabf34338940b936d40728ac9cdf45907feb67928300\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRRi1AA\"}"}